   "id": "45:141c",
   "op": "text",
   "en": "The masked woman stared fixedly at me.\nThe mask had no mouth. There were only two thin slits open around the eyes.\n\"Now, answer my questions, will you?\"\nThe thing spoke to me.\nThis time it wasn't the voice that spoke straight into my head like before. It was a clear, real voice.\nAnd how eerie that voice was.\nIt was like the noise you hear when you fast-forward a tape.\nThat was what it sounded like.\nShrill, yet strangely muffled, as if it had an echo on it. It was a voice that clung horribly to my ears.\nWas she waiting for my answer to what she'd just asked?\nI swallowed the spit that had pooled in my mouth.{p}How should I answer?\n"
  },
